WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.600
SCP-001 is an O5’s tale.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.440
It makes sense, doesn’t it?

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:11.040
After all, regardless of the exact nature
of an SCP-001 proposal, there are always certain

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.960
things that remain the same.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.480
See if you can recall them all.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.800
Well, for starters, SCP-001s are all about
vital moments.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.760
Perhaps, like The Prototype or The Foundation
or the Sheaf of Papers or the Gate Guardian,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.600
they’re about the very origin of the SCP
Foundation itself.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.720
Perhaps, like the Ouroborous Cycle or When
Day Breaks or The World Gone Beautiful, they’re

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.120
about apocalyptic-style destruction - Or perhaps,
the rebirth.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:43.280
Perhaps, like Consensus Reality or the Database,
they are rules or realizations that changed

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.160
everything.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.880
Maybe, like the Scarlet King or the Black
Moon or A Simple Toymaker, they’re about

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:53.360
the sparking of great rivalries that truly
define the backbone of the Foundation’s

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.320
activities.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:59.600
Another vital element of SCP-001 is always
secrecy and classification.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.480
They’re the most clandestine anomalies out
there, generally hidden away below layer after

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.880
layer of encryption and security.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:12.480
Even the database for SCP-001 entries is guarded
by a memetic kill agent that’ll leave you

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.880
stone dead on the ground if you’re below
that magical Level 5 clearance when you attempt

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:18.000
to access it.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.640
No information is more carefully and forcefully
guarded than this.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.040
And of course, another vital element of the
SCP-001 entry is deception and trickery.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.440
It’s inherent to the designation.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.320
No other number has multiple, entirely distinct&nbsp;

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.040
anomalies, many of which&nbsp;
either have no correlation

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:40.640
with one another or even actively contradict
each other.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.840
If you ask some people, they’ll tell you
there are multiple 001s, because each is of

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:51.520
equal importance in etching the rich portrait
of the Foundation’s past, present, and future.

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.360
Some would tell you something very different:
There’s only one SCP-001, it’s a shell

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:03.040
game, the rest are all fakes to stop people
from taking any single entry too seriously,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.680
and thus, forever avoiding the truth.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.480
Some, still, would tell you that there is
no SCP-001.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:14.960
It’s all just a complex web of lies meant
to keep the Foundation’s enemies and allies

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.280
in a state of pliable ignorance.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:23.040
If an intimate knowledge of the SCP Foundation’s
past and inner workings, a commitment to secrecy

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:28.320
at all costs, and a love of deception as a
tool for control all sound familiar, it’s

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.720
because they’re the favored tool kit of
a certain group we’re all familiar with:

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.840
The O5 Council, the very top brass of the
SCP Foundation.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:43.760
It only makes sense that if anyone knew the
truth about the fractured and strange SCP-001,

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.960
it would be them.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:49.440
The more observant among you may have also
noticed a certain omission from the many popular

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.760
SCP-001 entries we’ve name-dropped in this
video so far.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:59.920
And it’s no accident that this particular
SCP-001 entry is the only one straight from

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:05.040
the mouth of O5-1, the founder of the counsel,
himself.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.280
It is The Factory.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:12.480
It’s a strange and sordid tale of violence,
horror, and dark bargains made with truly

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.080
unknowable forces.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.960
It’s a tale that tells us about the initial
creation and growth of the Foundation, the

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.640
event that nearly destroyed it, and an indication
as to the dark future possibly in store.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.440
It’s a little bit of everything you can
expect from a good 001 proposal.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:35.760
And surely, if this is the SCP-001 entry that
the head of the council swears by, then it

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.760
must be the definitive entry into the 001
canon, right?

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:41.520
Well, not quite.

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:46.000
Because, as you’re about to find out, not
even the O5 Council itself can really reach

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.560
a consensus on the true nature of the fascinating
and much-feared Factory.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.920
But perhaps, through hearing every side of
this particularly dark story, we can find

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.280
the kernels of truth hiding somewhere in the
middle of it all.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:04.800
But of course, be warned, as with all things
when it comes to the O5 Council: It’s going

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.120
to get extremely weird.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.600
But before we move on to what the rest of
the O5 Council have to say about the factory,

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.800
it would be prudent to refresh our memory
on O5-1’s version of the story - The version

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:22.400
that has been considered to be absolute, before
we pore into the equally strange stories of

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.160
the other council members.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:29.200
It began with a wealthy industrialist and
thoroughly evil man named James Anderson all

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:35.440
the way back in 1835, when the United States
was still new and finding its feet.

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:42.240
Anderson was an engine of unchecked ambition,
malice, and most of all, truly boundless greed.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:47.360
He wanted everything and more, and being a
true businessman down to the core, he was

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.680
willing to make whatever deal he needed to
make in order to see himself become an even

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.880
wealthier man.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.280
That’s why, like a lot of bored rich people
in his day, he began dabbling in the dark

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.280
arts for fun and profit.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:04.480
Until, eventually, he made contact with a
benefactor on the other side.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:08.000
Under these instructions, James Anderson built
The Factory.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.280
A truly magnificent and&nbsp;
terrible feat of architecture&nbsp;

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.120
and engineering for the time.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:18.240
A multi-level, town-sized complex that could
produce everything from food to weapons to

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.800
toys to textiles to precious metals, and so
much more.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.760
Workers could find room and board at this
grand Factory and pay for it with their labor.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:33.200
For the would-be workers of an unsteady early
America, Anderson seemed like a saint.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.840
People flocked from all over the country to
live and work in The Factory.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:42.720
But once they were locked behind the Factory’s
doors, they realized that James Anderson was

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:43.840
no saint.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:47.680
He was as bad or worse than any devil he served.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.160
The inside of the factory was a torturous
nightmare, where people were regularly worked

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:57.040
to death and then ground into meat that was
sold off all across the country.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:01.680
Anderson kept a brutal guard force to beat
down anyone resisting or not working hard

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:02.480
enough.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:07.600
Those who weren’t worked to death or executed
by the guards for some petty infraction could

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.320
potentially have an even worse fate in store
for them: Being dragged off and subjected

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:15.280
to occult experiments by Anderson.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:19.680
These people wouldn’t be killed, but they
would live as humans no more.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:23.760
Anderson was able to keep the Factory and
its nightmarish activities running and under

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:27.440
wraps for decades, all the way into the Civil
War.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:32.000
It was only when a beaten, bloody, starved,
and traumatized worker managed to escape and

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.800
alert President Ulysses S.&nbsp;
Grant of the mistreatment&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:37.840
going on inside that something was done about

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:38.400
it.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:44.240
This is where O5-1, and a progenitor of the
SCP Foundation, would get involved.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.240
There was a small but elite group of Union
Soldiers commissioned by President Grant to

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:53.760
work behind the Confederate Lines, specializing
in tackling the strange and supernatural down

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:54.480
South.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.440
This group, of course, was led by O5-1.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.760
Considering some of the reports of anomalous
supernatural activity going on behind the

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.720
closed doors of the Anderson Factory, Grant
knew that these would be the men to send on

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:08.080
this vital mission.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.520
And President Grant’s faith in these men
was rewarded.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:16.240
Though it wasn’t an easy fight, they were
able to infiltrate and defeat the forces of

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:17.120
the Factory.

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.600
They fought their way through Anderson’s
sadistic guards, through his menagerie of

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:27.120
terrifying homemade monsters, and eventually,
they got to Anderson himself.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.120
They were so appalled by the horrors they’d
seen inside the Factory, they couldn’t stop

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:36.000
themselves from torturing Anderson to death,
and dismembering his corpse.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.160
They freed the trapped workers and rooted
out whatever remained of Anderson’s forces

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.360
within the building.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.720
However, this is where they made their first
pivotal decision.

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:49.920
Rather than simply destroying the sordid place
and leaving it as rubble, they instead decided

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.920
to utilize it, and the many anomalous objects
that it produced.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.280
This became the foundation of the Foundation.

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:01.600
Over time, their organization grew and the
O5 Council was formed.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:05.520
They began spreading their influence and capturing
anomalies all over.

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:10.880
This was, however, until they engaged in a
bloody war with the superior military forces

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:11.920
of the Fae.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:16.880
Despite their augmented weaponry and tools
from the Factory, when the Fae performed an

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:20.000
all-out assault against them, they were decimated.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:25.680
In his greatest shame, O5-1 fled the battlefield
into the bowels of the Factory, as his friends

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.800
and allies were slaughtered by the Fae behind
him.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:33.840
Eventually, after locking himself in a room
with an ornate door, he encountered the true

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:39.360
demonic heart of the Factory, using Anderson’s
dismembered corpse as a mouthpiece.

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:42.880
O5-1 struck a terrible deal with the Factory.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:47.200
They wiped out the Fae entirely and reversed
all the damage they had done.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:52.240
The SCP Foundation grew beyond the Factory
and eventually covered it in rubble out of

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:52.880
shame.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.880
But the Factory wasn’t done.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.200
It is still very much alive and furious at
being betrayed.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:04.080
It will keep producing deadly anomalous objects
and creatures and releasing them out into

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:07.840
the world until the Foundation pays what it
owes in full.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:13.120
And the occasional sacrificed D-Class, Researcher,
and Guard won’t cut it forever…

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.760
Or, at least, that’s how O5-1 tells it.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:19.680
It’s a chilling story, but can it really
be called a complete one?

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:23.600
We wanted to find out for ourselves, which
is why we asked every other member of the

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.120
O5 Council to tell their side of the Factory’s
tale.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.320
These are 12 Tales About a Factory.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.760
O5-2, upon being asked, went white as a sheet.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:38.320
He cleared his throat and made the admission
that, in truth, the Factory came back with

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:38.800
him.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.880
As it turns out, O5-2 was a time traveler
from the future.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:48.480
Back in his native time, an alternate timeline
of the present, he was a mere researcher,

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.080
until an accident led to him being completely
unmoored from time.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:54.880
He was thrown all over the temporal landscape.

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:57.760
He saw civilizations rise and fall.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.080
He took the time to hang out with Jesus.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.680
He was a pretty chill guy.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:06.640
And ultimately, he decided the best way to
use his bizarre new condition was to help

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.040
better the future with his knowledge.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:13.840
One piece of technology he brought back was
a hyper-advanced piece of technology known

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.680
as a nanofactory.

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:20.880
Which, as the name suggests, is a machine
that uses nanobots to construct pretty much

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:24.240
anything - like the ultimate futuristic 3D
printer.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:29.440
It resulted in the creation of a huge number
of futuristic items that helped the SCP Foundation

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:34.160
along in their mission to secure, contain,
and protect, including amnestics.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:40.240
However, what O5-2 didn’t realize was that
a rogue AI was also nested in the nanofactory,

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.320
and this AI soon went berserk.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:47.760
As a result, the nanofactory became The Factory,
producing dangerous anomalies with reckless

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:52.960
abandon, to the detriment of both the SCP
Foundation and the world at large.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.000
On the whole, it was somewhat of a mixed bag.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:59.600
O5-3 seemed a little spaced-out about even
being asked.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.920
He claimed that he was there to witness the
very birth of the Factory, but it didn’t

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:08.080
happen in reality as we know it - It happened
in cyberspace.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:12.400
He and his colleagues were very interested
in the Matrix-esque journey of downloading

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:17.600
their minds into computers back in the day
- Both for practical reasons and to play extremely

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:19.200
immersive games of Doom.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:22.640
However, one day, something fundamentally
changed.

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:26.480
A new consciousness was born in then-Soviet
Russia.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:32.480
O5-3 and two of his companions, all operating
in cyberspace, went to go check it out, along

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.960
with a few helpful AI constructs.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:40.560
Eventually, they discovered it, an ever-expanding
data packet that would transform into a powerful

00:11:40.560 --> 00:11:46.880
artificial consciousness known as The Factory,
with mysterious motives and seemingly malicious

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.680
intent.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:53.040
Something it more than proved when it erased
the mind of one of O5-3’s companions, killing

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:53.680
him.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:57.360
Since this incident, the Factory has only
gotten more powerful.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:02.720
Its modus operandi is affecting machines in
the real world and causing them to produce

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:08.560
anomalous items, which then become the SCP
Foundation’s latest problems to deal with.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:13.600
O5-4 seemed both twitchy and indignant when
the topic was brought up.

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:18.000
They lamented the fact that the Foundation
hadn’t put more research into the Factory

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.880
and how to stop it, because technically, it’s
their most dangerous and mysterious enemy

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:23.920
group of interest.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:30.640
O5-4 explained it as follows: The FBI Unusual
Incidents Unit is a joke, Are We Cool Yet?

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:35.440
Is just a bunch of pretentious, privileged
rich kids, Marshall, Carter, and Dark, Ltd.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.560
only care about money and thus can be bought
off.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:43.680
The Global Occult Coalition often helps them
take care of more challenging anomalies.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:48.240
The Church of the Broken God and the Sarkicists
are often too busy waging petty religious

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.040
wars against each other to do real, meaningful
damage to the SCP Foundation.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:58.880
Prometheus Labs had already fallen, and Dr.
Wondertainment wouldn’t thrive forever.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:02.640
The Factory, however, was a truly unknown
quantity.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:08.560
It’s just out there, somewhere, pumping
out anomalies that soon become everyone else’s

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:10.400
very dangerous problem.

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:15.920
O5-4 personally resented that the Foundation
and their fellow council members don’t see

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:21.440
this and allocate more resources to the cause
because someday soon, it might really come

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:24.800
back to bite them - as these things often
do.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.360
O5-5 was considerably bitter.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:33.440
As in, they denied that the factory ever existed,
claimed that the SCP Foundation made it up

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:37.920
to cover up a bunch of anomalies that they
themselves had created, and then told us to…

00:13:38.680 --> 00:13:40.560
Ahem, “eff off.”

00:13:40.560 --> 00:13:41.440
If you know what I mean.

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:49.600
Tsk, tsk, some people get so hostile when
you just want simple answers…

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:55.840
Next came the tale of 05-6, which came in
the form of a World War II espionage anecdote.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:14:00.240
Of course, this was also during the height
of the Seventh Occult War, and Hitler, assisted

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:04.720
by the Thule Society and the Obskurakorps,
was trying to get his greasy little hands

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:09.600
on as many anomalies as possible in hopes
of turning the tide of the war in his favor.

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:16.880
O5-6 was working undercover behind enemy lines,
disguised as an SS officer, as he slowly helped

00:14:16.880 --> 00:14:20.400
dismantle Hitler’s anomalous offensive from
within.

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:24.800
He’d heard whisperings of the Nazis developing
a weapon unlike any other.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:30.320
A Factory that would produce anomalies for
them on-demand and give them the supernatural

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.040
edge.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:36.320
O5-6 didn’t believe it at first, until he
was attacked by a group of vicious, living

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:39.440
Punch and Judy dolls
created by the factory.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:43.760
He narrowly managed to survive the ambush,
but seemed disturbed in recounting the fact

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:47.200
that when he destroyed the dolls, they bled
profusely.

00:14:47.200 --> 00:14:51.280
Eventually, the leads he was following led
him to a ruin at the base of Zugspitze.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:57.840
Inside, he discovered the ruin was hollow,
and filled with floating stone orbs - producing

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:02.320
energy that allowed the Thule Society Researchers
to produce more anomalies.

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:10.320
O5-6 was able to destroy this anomaly factory,
but he took a souvenir: SCP-627, a little

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:14.720
stone ball that rolls around on the ground
when it comes in contact with people.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:20.720
O5-7 admitted, somewhat sheepishly, that while
there was technically no real physical Factory,

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:24.560
Factory product anomalies are real, and they’re
all his fault.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:29.280
He purchased a bunch of random items from
Walmart and printed a fake logo for “The

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.480
Factory” on the back.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:35.280
His plan was to give these totally innocent
objects to Junior Researchers, both to mess

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:38.720
with them for fun and to test their critical
thinking skills.

00:15:38.720 --> 00:15:44.080
However, it turned out that simply placing
this logo onto an item results in it becoming

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:45.680
an anomalous item.

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:50.880
Admittedly, it was rough for O5-7 to have
to follow the cool story about fighting magic

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:51.760
Nazis.

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:57.680
O5-8 made the far more exciting claim that
the Factory is actually all the way up on

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:58.560
the moon.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:03.440
Back when the SCP Foundation were first founding
Moon Base Alpha, they discovered that some

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:08.400
ancient and unknown civilization had already
built a covert base under the surface.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:11.840
It was a storehouse of anomalous alien technology.

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:14.160
The first thirteen people&nbsp;
to enter were immediately&nbsp;

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.720
vaporized by the laser defense system, but

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:20.240
the fourth to enter was given an even worse
fate.

00:16:20.240 --> 00:16:26.000
He was pulled into the machine and fused with
it, at which point, the Factory was truly

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:26.960
activated.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:32.240
It began to produce anomalies and transport
them to random locations all across the globe,

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.720
and it’s been a problem since.

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:39.760
When we spoke to O5-9 on the matter, with
a steely look in his eye, he simply muttered

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:41.520
the word, “Atlantis.”

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.920
No further comments were made on the matter.

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:50.560
O5-10 explained that the Factory was a single
man, a truly ancient and brilliant anomalous

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:54.000
craftsman that they found in a mountain temple
in Tibet.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:58.720
He was taken by the Foundation and contained,
but given far more high-tech tools to work

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:02.800
his magic so they could keep reaping the anomalous
fruits of his labors.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:07.840
However, the craftsman was appropriately crafty,
and managed to produce a duplicate of himself

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:10.480
to distract the Foundation while he made an
escape.

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:16.320
He’s still out there to this day, making
more anomalies, a one-man Factory.

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:21.920
O5-11 claimed that the Factory was alien in
origin, but it wasn’t on the moon.

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:28.000
It was the true explanation for the iconic
1947 Roswell, New Mexico, UFO incident.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:33.280
A flying saucer descended and offered O5-11,
who was the Commander of the response team

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.760
at the time, the most wonderful things.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:41.040
This saucer became the Factory, but humanity
and O5-11 were deceived.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:46.160
It wasn’t long before this extraterrestrial
factory was producing countless deadly anomalous

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:50.160
nightmares the world over, with nothing we
could do about it.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:53.360
O5-12 said that the Factory is a mess.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:58.320
It’s a remnant of the Foundation’s attempt
to erase the supernatural from human belief.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:03.120
Foundation Researchers claim that due to the
inherent power in human belief, the belief

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:08.160
in the supernatural gave it power, and phasing
humanity as a whole out of this belief was

00:18:08.160 --> 00:18:12.560
a major factor in making sure things weren’t
much worse than they are today.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:17.360
However, some hardy things slipped through
the cracks, and because reality has a strange

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:21.760
sense of humor, these things are marked with
the logo of the Factory.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:27.360
To round things off, we have a bonus tale
from the mysterious O5-13 - who was instrumental

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.840
in helping us put the rest of this video together.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:35.040
He claims that he created the Factory, and
that it acts as a kind of countermeasure against

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.960
interdimensional invaders.

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:41.840
While it may seem like the factory is creating
anomalies, it’s actually intercepting them,

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:43.600
and making them safer.

00:18:43.600 --> 00:18:48.480
Some anomalies that seem to come from the
Factory may be dangerous, but if O5-13 is

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:53.200
to be believed, then they’d be a hell of
a lot more dangerous if the Factory wasn’t

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:53.920
here.

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:58.880
And there you have it, folks, the story of
the Factory from every possible angle - Even

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:02.880
though it feels like each angle is facing
in an entirely different direction.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:07.040
In the words of Oprah Winfrey, “So, what
is the truth?”

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:11.600
Is there a nugget of reality beneath all the
fallacy, or do you think the O5 Council was

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:14.080
trolling all of us for even daring to ask?

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:16.880
We leave that question to you, dear viewers.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.920
Let us know which theory you believe down
in the comments below.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:26.480
Now go check out “Children of SCP-001 The
Scarlet King - Is SCP-999 Really His Son?”

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:32.320
and “SCP-001 The Ouroboros Cycle - The Full
Epic Story Explained” for more tales of

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:34.000
the frightening, mysterious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:37.840
and always fascinating
anomaly SCP-001!

